#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: openWB"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"openWB is a wallbox with its own charging control (software “openWB 2”). "
"There are **two independent connections** between openWB and OpenEMS, one in "
"each direction:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Direction\n"
"| Who reads whom?\n"
"| Route\n"
"| Controls anything?\n"
"\n"
"| openWB reads OpenEMS\n"
"| openWB queries grid, PV and storage from OpenEMS to charge with surplus\n"
"| REST interface of OpenEMS (port 8084)\n"
"| no\n"
"| OpenEMS reads openWB\n"
"| OpenEMS adopts the power and state of an openWB charge point\n"
"| MQTT broker of openWB\n"
"| no\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"The basis is the source code of openWB 2 (“core”) and the OpenEMS source "
"code. Neither of the two connections has been tried out here. The page "
"xref:user/third-party/overview.adoc[Third-party systems on OpenEMS] gives a "
"comparison with Home Assistant and evcc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "openWB reads OpenEMS"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"In openWB, there is the device **“openEMS, Fenecon FEMS, CENTURIO 10, Kaco "
"Hy-Control”** for this. Only the **IP address** of the system and the "
"**password** need to be entered. openWB always uses “x” as the user name; "
"with OpenEMS only the password counts."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid "You create up to three components for the device:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Component in openWB\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| Meter\n"
"| Grid connection (utility meter)\n"
"| Inverter\n"
"| PV production\n"
"| Storage\n"
"| Home battery; setting “Number”: 1 = `+ess0+`, any other number = `+ess2+`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"**Prerequisite in OpenEMS:** the app or component “REST/JSON API read "
"access” (Controller.Api.Rest.ReadOnly) or “… read/write access” on the "
"default port **8084**. openWB always queries this port. According to the "
"OpenEMS code, reading already works with the Guest role. See xref:user/"
"external-interfaces/rest-control.adoc[Control via REST/JSON]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| openWB component\n"
"| Value in openWB\n"
"| Channel in OpenEMS\n"
"\n"
".5+| Meter\n"
"| Total power and per phase\n"
"| `+meter0/ActivePower+`, `+ActivePowerL1…L3+`\n"
"| Voltage per phase\n"
"| `+meter0/VoltageL1…L3+`\n"
"| Frequency\n"
"| `+meter0/Frequency+`\n"
"| Purchase (meter reading)\n"
"| `+_sum/GridBuyActiveEnergy+`\n"
"| Feed-in (meter reading)\n"
"| `+_sum/GridSellActiveEnergy+`\n"
".2+| Inverter\n"
"| Power\n"
"| `+_sum/ProductionActivePower+` (sign inverted)\n"
"| Meter reading\n"
"| `+_sum/ProductionActiveEnergy+`\n"
".3+| Storage\n"
"| State of charge\n"
"| `+ess0/Soc+` or `+ess2/Soc+`\n"
"| Charge and discharge energy\n"
"| `+ess0/DcChargeEnergy+`, `+DcDischargeEnergy+`\n"
"| Power\n"
"| **calculated** from `+_sum+`: grid {plus} production − consumption\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"openWB reads units (e.g. W or kW) from the response and converts them. The "
"values are queried in each openWB control cycle (default 10 seconds)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How it queries"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-it-queries
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"openWB uses the OpenEMS option of reading several values in one request with "
"**patterns** (regular expressions), e.g. all matching values of `+meter0+` "
"and `+_sum+` at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-it-queries
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"At startup, openWB checks whether the system understands patterns across "
"components. If so, **one** request per component is sufficient; otherwise "
"openWB splits the query into several requests. The current OpenEMS code "
"understands both."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-it-queries
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"A comment in the openWB code says that systems should not be queried too "
"often with the combined query."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"**Fixed names:** openWB assumes that the grid meter is called `+meter0+` and "
"the storage `+ess0+` (or `+ess2+`). With different naming, for example if "
"`+meter0+` is a consumption meter, the values are not correct."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"**Storage power is derived:** It does not come from the storage itself, but "
"from the total values. With several storage systems, it is the sum of all, "
"but the state of charge is only that of `+ess0+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"**Inverter = total production:** The sum of all PV sources is read (AC and "
"DC), not an individual inverter."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"**Read only:** openWB does not control anything in OpenEMS via this "
"connection, not even the storage."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"**Port fixed at 8084:** If the REST interface runs on another port or only "
"behind a proxy, the connection does not work."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"**Unencrypted:** HTTP with basic authentication; the password goes through "
"the network in plain text."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"In the openWB code, a fallback route for the meter was noticed, intended for "
"very old systems without pattern queries. It accesses a password field that "
"the meter component does not set anywhere. In Python, such an access aborts "
"with an error, so the fallback route cannot work. This route is not used "
"with current OpenEMS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS reads openWB"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS has the component **“EVCS OpenWB”** (Evcs.OpenWB). It reads an "
"internal charge point of an openWB series 2. This additionally requires a "
"**“Bridge MQTT”**, which is connected to the MQTT broker of the openWB."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Setting\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| MQTT Bridge ID\n"
"| ID of the MQTT bridge (default `+mqtt0+`)\n"
"| Chargepoint\n"
"| internal charge point 0 or 1 (with openWB Duo two charge points)\n"
"| Phase rotation\n"
"| Phase rotation of the connection\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"The MQTT bridge needs the address and port of the broker. In the "
"configuration of openWB 2, the broker can be reached in insecure mode on "
"port **1883** without login, in secure mode encrypted on port **8883**. "
"Reading is permitted for everyone (`+openWB/#+`). For secure mode, openWB "
"sets up a self-signed certificate (Debian's “snakeoil” certificate). The "
"OpenEMS MQTT bridge has fields for its own certificate store (“Trust Store”, "
"“Key Store”), but does not evaluate them in the code. It only trusts the "
"root certificates delivered with Java. A self-signed certificate is not one "
"of them, so the encrypted connection to the openWB is not established. The "
"unencrypted port 1883 remains for the bridge."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-which-values-are-read-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS subscribes to the messages under `+openWB/internal_chargepoint/0/"
"get/…+` (or `+…/1/…+`) and adopts:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| openWB message\n"
"| Value in OpenEMS\n"
"\n"
"| power, powers\n"
"| Charging power total and per phase\n"
"| voltages, currents\n"
"| Voltage and current per phase\n"
"| imported\n"
"| Energy meter (charged energy) and from this the energy of the charging session\n"
"| plug_state, charge_state\n"
"| Plug inserted, charging\n"
"| phases_in_use\n"
"| Phases used\n"
"| fault_state\n"
"| Fault state\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"The charge point appears in OpenEMS as a **metered consumer** and is thus "
"included in consumption and energy flows (see xref:user/basics/energy-"
"flows.adoc[Energy flows])."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"**Read only:** The component is a pure measured-value charge point. OpenEMS "
"can therefore **not control** the openWB (no surplus charging by OpenEMS, no "
"power specification). In this combination, surplus charging is done by the "
"openWB itself, with the values from the first section."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"Only **internal** charge points of the openWB, no other charge points "
"managed by the openWB."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid "The energy meter of the openWB is adopted as an absolute meter reading."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"In OpenEMS, there is no app in the app center for openWB; the bridge and "
"component are created as components."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"**Can openWB control the OpenEMS storage, e.g. not discharge into the car?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"Not via this connection; openWB only reads. Such behavior must be set in "
"OpenEMS itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid "**openWB shows wrong grid values.**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"Check whether the grid meter in OpenEMS is really called `+meter0+`. openWB "
"always queries this name."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid "**Do I need the OpenEMS write app for openWB?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"No. The read app is sufficient for openWB; for OpenEMS → openWB, no REST app "
"is needed, but the MQTT bridge."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid "**Do both systems charge with surplus at the same time?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
msgid ""
"If OpenEMS only reads the openWB (as above), the openWB alone controls. If "
"you also use surplus charging in OpenEMS for other charge points, bear in "
"mind that both systems see the same surplus (see xref:user/ev-charging-"
"control/surplus-charging.adoc[Surplus charging])."
msgstr ""
